.TH APPMGR 1 "November 2026" "appmgr 2.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appmgr \- Universal application combine for .deb, .AppImage, binary archives (.tar.*, .zip), and standalone ELF binaries with Package Registry and GitHub integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appmgr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appmgr
is a hybrid package management combine that brings the aesthetics of Pacman together with the granular dependency analysis and triggers of APT. It accurately installs and manages standalone Debian (.deb) packages, AppImage (.AppImage) binaries, binary archives (.tar.xz, .tar.zst, .tar.gz, .tgz, .tar.bz2, .zip), and raw standalone ELF binaries into isolated directories, automatically creates application wrappers, configures desktop shortcuts for GUI apps, extracts icons, and updates system caches. It supports declarative package registries (sources.list) with Schema v2 TOML source recipes, direct downloads, HTTP 302 redirects, GitHub Search and Releases APIs, multithreaded upgrade checking, SHA-256 verification, version pinning, rollback caching, environment variables and arguments management, and JSON manifest export/import.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinstall\fR, \fBi\fR \fITARGET\fR [\fI--repo OWNER/REPO\fR] [\fI--prefer appimage|deb|tar|zip|bin\fR] [\fI--pre\fR] [\fI-y\fR] [\fI--auto-deps\fR] [\fI--no-deps\fR] [\fI--rootless-deps\fR]
Installs a package with automatic target detection:
1. If \fITARGET\fR is an existing local file (.deb, .AppImage, .tar.*, .zip, or standalone ELF binary), installs it locally.
2. If \fITARGET\fR ends with \fB.toml\fR, parses and installs directly from the declarative recipe.
3. If \fITARGET\fR matches a package ID in active registries, installs according to the recipe's source configuration.
4. If \fITARGET\fR is a URL, \fBgithub:owner/repo[@tag]\fR, or in \fBowner/repo[@tag]\fR format, installs directly from GitHub Releases.
5. Otherwise, treats \fITARGET\fR as an application name and searches GitHub repositories, presenting an interactive selection menu.
Automatically filters assets by host architecture, validates SHA-256 checksums if available, cleans launcher names, sets up desktop integration, and performs automatic 2-tier shared library dependency resolution (host package manager + rootless sandbox pool).
.TP
\fBdeps\fR [\fIAPP\fR] [\fI--all\fR] [\fI--fix\fR] [\fI--auto-deps\fR] [\fI--rootless-deps\fR]
Inspects or repairs dynamic shared library (.so) dependencies for installed applications.
With \fI--fix\fR, automatically resolves missing dependencies via native host packages (Tier 1) or downloads rootless library bundles into the application's isolated sandbox (Tier 2).
.TP
\fBsearch\fR, \fBs\fR, \fBfind\fR \fIQUERY\fR [\fI--source ID\fR] [\fI--driver TYPE\fR] [\fI--offline\fR]
Searches local package registry databases and upstream GitHub repositories for applications matching \fIQUERY\fR.
.TP
\fBupdate\fR, \fBsync\fR
Synchronizes local repository databases from configured package registries in sources.list using ETag caching and concurrent retrieval.
.TP
\fBrepo\fR, \fBsources\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manages package repositories in \fB~/.config/appmgr/sources.list\fR (or \fB/etc/appmgr/sources.list\fR).
Subcommands: \fBlist [--json]\fR, \fBadd <driver> <id> <url>\fR, \fBremove <id>\fR, \fBenable <id>\fR, \fBdisable <id>\fR.
.TP
\fBsource\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Validates and tests Schema v2 TOML source definitions.
Subcommands: \fBlint <file.toml>\fR, \fBtest <file.toml>\fR.
.TP
\fBpkg\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Maintainer tools for Schema v2 source recipe creation, validation, and testing.
Subcommands:
- \fBnew <id> [-o file.toml]\fR: Generates a Schema v2 TOML source recipe template.
- \fBlint <file.toml>\fR: Validates a recipe against Schema v2 constraints.
- \fBtest <file.toml> [--dry-run]\fR: Tests upstream URL reachability and index access.
.TP
\fBlink\fR \fIAPP\fR \fIOWNER/REPO\fR
Links an existing installed application to a GitHub repository to track future releases and updates.
.TP
\fBupgrade\fR, \fBup\fR [\fIAPP\fR] [\fI--check\fR] [\fI--prefer appimage|deb|tar|zip|bin\fR] [\fI--pre\fR] [\fI--force\fR] [\fI--json\fR] [\fI-y\fR]
Checks for newer releases across linked repositories and registry recipes using concurrent multithreading and ETag caching. Preserves custom env vars and persistent launch args.
.TP
\fBrollback\fR \fIAPP\fR [\fI-y\fR]
Restores the previous version of an application from the local rollback cache, restoring files, launchers, shortcuts, and metadata.
.TP
\fBclean\fR [\fI-y\fR]
Cleans up the rollback cache, temporary downloads, and orphaned directories, reporting total freed disk space.
.TP
\fBenv\fR \fIAPP\fR [\fIKEY=VALUE ...\fR] [\fI--unset KEY\fR] [\fI--list\fR]
Manages custom environment variables for an application and regenerates its launcher wrapper.
.TP
\fBargs\fR \fIAPP\fR [\fIFLAGS ...\fR] [\fI--clear\fR] [\fI--list\fR]
Configures persistent CLI arguments for an application that are automatically passed on every launch.
.TP
\fBpin\fR \fIAPP\fR
Freezes an application to its current version, preventing general upgrades from modifying it.
.TP
\fBunpin\fR \fIAPP\fR
Unfreezes an application, re-enabling automatic updates during upgrade.
.TP
\fBexport\fR [\fIFILE.json\fR]
Exports all installed applications, formats, repository links, env vars, and launch flags into a JSON manifest file.
.TP
\fBimport\fR \fIFILE.json\fR [\fI-y\fR]
Reads a JSON manifest file, installs missing applications from GitHub or registries, and applies their pin, env, and args.
.TP
\fBremove\fR, \fBrm\fR, \fBuninstall\fR \fINAME\fR [\fI-y\fR]
Uninstalls an application, removing all files, launchers, icons, and desktop entries.
.TP
\fBlist\fR, \fBls\fR [\fI--type TYPE\fR] [\fI--json\fR]
Displays a table of all managed applications, versions, formats ([DEB], [APPIMAGE], [TAR], [ZIP], [BIN]), pinned status, and installed sizes.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR \fITARGET\fR
Displays metadata, installed location, launch commands, repository origin, and performs shared library (ldd) dependency verification.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR, \fBcheck\fR
Runs a comprehensive system diagnostic: checks archive tools (tar, xz, zstd), FUSE status, Bubblewrap virtualization, PATH integrity, desktop indexers, broken launchers, and static/dynamic binary dependencies.
.TP
\fBrun\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
Launches an application with its configured environment and persistent arguments.
.TP
\fBupdate-db\fR
Forces update of desktop menu databases and icon theme caches.
.TP
\fBself-update\fR [\fI--check\fR] [\fI--pre\fR] [\fI-y\fR]
Updates the \fBappmgr\fR binary from GitHub Releases (disabled when built without \fBself-update\fR feature or managed by pacman).
.TP
\fBcompletions\fR \fISHELL\fR
Generates shell completions (\fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, \fBfish\fR) to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR, \fB--noconfirm\fR
Assume yes to all prompts and non-interactively select the default choices.
.TP
\fB--user\fR
Install into user home directory (~/.local) without requiring root/sudo privileges.
.TP
\fB--system\fR
Install system-wide into /opt/appmgr/apps and /usr/local/bin (requires root/sudo).
.TP
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
Show version and exit.
